findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged from_file_or_default using unwrap_or_default() to swallow
    all error types. TEA mentioned 'no silent error swallowing' in security test descriptions
    but wrote no test targeting the NotFound vs parse/permission error distinction.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote security tests for CWE-209: ''Error messages don''t leak connection
    strings, passwords, or internal details.'' Dev implemented sanitized Display impls.
    Reviewer verified (#11) as ''properly handled.'' However, the Io(#[error(transparent)])
    specific leak path may not be fully covered, so this is a weak catch.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA and Dev addressed CWE-113 header injection via newline rejection\
    \ in with_tenant/with_token, but the core finding \u2014 using raw String instead\
    \ of validated TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not caught. Reviewer even\
    \ noted (#8) axiathon-core is declared but unused, yet did not connect this to\
    \ the tenant_id type safety gap."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the 6 dependencies using direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Dev even added chrono and uuid with direct versions. Reviewer
    did not check Cargo.toml dependency declarations against workspace conventions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer observation #4 [MEDIUM]: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown\
    \ fields \u2014 no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]... operator typos will silently\
    \ be treated as defaults. No test covers this behavior.' Directly matches the\
    \ finding about token field being silently ignored."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern. Neither TEA nor Reviewer audited test assertion logic for tautological
    conditions.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic via
    ''let _ = config;''. Despite SOUL.md principle #4 (''A vacuously true test is
    worse than no test''), no phase audited test assertion density.'
